\end{align*}
where the last expression separates out the $\mathcal{I} = [k]$ term, ensures all other terms have a negative sign, and bounds their magnitude from above.
Using parts \ref{item:cN_property1} and \ref{item:cN_property4} of Proposition~\ref{thm:cN_properties} to upper bound all but one of the $c_N(\tau_N(t_{j-1})) + \sum c_N(s)^2 \leq t + 2$ factors, arbitrarily setting $j^\star(\mathcal{I}) := \min\{j \notin \mathcal{I} \}$, as well as recalling that $\sum_{ j = 1 }^k (i_j - i_{j - 1}) = k$ and $|\mathcal{I}^c| \leq k$, this is further bounded by
\begin{align*}
